<!--T:1-->
== In scope ==
{| class="wikitable"
! Kind !! Id !! An item is
|-
| <code>category</code> || Page id of the category page || A page created while it is in the category. Pages added to the category later are not items.
|-
| <code>section</code> || Page id || A section at the page's unit level whose heading path was not in the previous revision. Edits by bots count.
|}

<!--T:2-->
=== section ===
The page sets its unit with <code><nowiki>{{FEDIFEEDSNAME:</nowiki>&lt;name&gt;|section-unit=&lt;n&gt;}}</code>: each heading with this many equals signs is one note. The default is 2, so each <code>== heading ==</code> is one note. A heading with more equals signs belongs to the note above it, and a heading with fewer is context for the notes below it.

<!--T:7-->
An item is identified by the page id and its heading path: the texts of the headings above it and its own. The paths of the parent revision and the new revision are compared. Renaming the heading or any heading above it therefore removes one item and adds another.

<!--T:8-->
A path can occur more than once, as when two sections under the same heading have the same title. Paths are then counted: when the new revision has a path more times than the parent, each extra occurrence is a new item, numbered in the order they appeared. An item exists while the page has its path at least as many times as its number.

<!--T:9-->
For example, a log of updates where each day is a section and each update a section in it, both newest first, sets <code>section-unit=3</code>:
<syntaxhighlight lang="text">
{{FEDIFEEDSNAME:Updates|section|section-unit=3}}
== 19 October ==
=== 14:10 ===
[https://example.org/changes/2 Change 2]
* Updated the search
==== Added ====
* A new page
=== 09:00 ===
[https://example.org/changes/1 Change 1]
== 18 October ==
=== 14:10 ===
[https://example.org/changes/0 Change 0]
</syntaxhighlight>

<!--T:10-->
Each update is an item, with a path such as "19 October / 14:10". Adding a new day with its first update makes one item, the update, and the day is its context. The <code>14:10</code> under 19 October is a different item from the one under 18 October. <code>==== Added ====</code> is part of its update's note. Two updates in the same minute make the path "19 October / 14:10" twice, and the second is item number 2 of that path.

<!--T:6-->
Only a save to an existing page is compared. The headings of a page's first revision are not items, because it has no parent revision. A null edit adds nothing, and neither does a revert, which brings back headings that were there before.

<!--T:11-->
=== Translations ===
On a wiki with [<tvar name="1">https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Special:MyLanguage/Extension:Translate</tvar> Extension:Translate], a page marked for translation gets a translation page for each language, such as <code>Post/en</code>, which keeps the page's categories. A translation page is never an item of a <code>category</code> feed, and neither is the page in the source language, such as <code>Post/ko</code>, that Translate may make. Otherwise each translation would be a second post, sent as soon as its first unit was saved and mostly in the source language.

<!--T:12-->
Instead each category has a feed for each language, <code>category_&lt;language&gt;_&lt;id&gt;</code>, named as the category's feed is with the language added, and with followers of its own. A translation page is an item of its language's feed of each category it is in, once, when its translation is complete: every unit, the title included when it is translated, has a translation that is not outdated. This is checked each time Translate saves the translation page, which it does after each unit is translated. A translation that falls behind later, as when the page gains a unit, sends nothing, and completing it again sends nothing either. A category that a translation page names as <code>Category:Posts/en</code>, as <code><nowiki>[[Category:Posts{{#translation:}}]]</nowiki></code> does, counts as <code>Category:Posts</code> when it is that category's translation page. Without Translate no page is a translation page, and the language feeds have no items.

<!--T:13-->
A translation page has no <code>section</code> items, since its headings change from the source language's as its units are translated.

<!--T:3-->
== Reserved ==
These names are kept so that later kinds do not collide. None of them is planned.

<!--T:4-->
{| class="wikitable"
! Kind !! An item is
|-
| <code>category_added</code> || A page added to the category, including existing pages and pages categorised by a template
|-
| <code>category_file</code> || A file added to the category
|-
| <code>page</code> || An edit to the page
|-
| <code>stable</code> || A newly reviewed revision of the page (FlaggedRevs)
|-
| <code>related</code> || An edit to a page the page links to
|-
| <code>file</code> || A new version of a file
|-
| <code>user_new</code> || A page created by the user
|-
| <code>user_upload</code> || A file uploaded by the user
|-
| <code>user_achievements</code> || A badge the user receives (AchievementBadges)
|-
| <code>namespace_new</code> || A new page in the namespace; the id is the namespace number
|-
| <code>topics</code> || A new topic on a talk page (DiscussionTools)
|-
| <code>newsletter</code> || A new issue of a newsletter (Newsletter)
|}

<!--T:5-->
== Never ==
These would publish something private, or turn a feed into a way to follow a person around: watchlists, notifications, thanks, block and abuse filter logs, CheckUser, the account creation log, and a feed of every edit by one user.
</translate>

